Changes from upstream github.com/luthermonson/go-proxmox
========================================================

This file records the modifications made in this fork, as required by
section 4(b) of the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The upstream project at github.com/luthermonson/go-proxmox is the canonical
source. Use it unless you specifically need this fork.


2026-09-18  Forked from github.com/luthermonson/go-proxmox at commit
            f9f8ec1c961caca60dcf02adcabda7cb2b5d6530.

            Up to and including that commit the contents of this
            repository are identical to upstream.

2026-09-18  Renamed the Go module path from
            github.com/luthermonson/go-proxmox to
            github.com/suykerbuyk/go-proxmox.

            Changed, 107 files:
              - go.mod: the module declaration.
              - 101 .go files: the self-import path only. No program
                logic, no exported identifier and no behaviour was
                changed by this commit.
              - examples/sdn/go.mod, examples/term-and-vnc/go.mod and
                examples/vm-template/go.mod: the replace and require
                paths of the three nested example modules.
              - AGENTS.md and README.md: documentation references to the
                import path, and the repository-status badges.

            Deliberately NOT changed, so that they keep pointing at the
            upstream project they describe:
              - proxmox.go:502, a doc comment citing upstream issue
                luthermonson/go-proxmox#221, which does not exist here.
              - migration/v0.6.0.md, migration/v0.7.0.md and
                migration/v0.7.1.md: historical links to upstream pull
                requests and issues.
              - README.md links to five unrelated upstream repositories.

            Removed: the codecov badge from README.md. It embedded a
            repository token belonging to the upstream project, which
            does not apply to this fork.

2026-09-19  fix(vm): VirtualMachine.Delete and UnmountCloudInitISO no
            longer delete the VM when the cloud-init ISO's lookup fails
            on a storage that may hold it. When a lookup fails, the
            storage's content listing decides: a listing that shows the
            ISO, cannot be read, or carries no data stops the delete with
            an error and no VM DELETE is sent; a listing without the ISO
            skips the storage, as before. A lookup that finds the ISO
            still deletes it.

            Changed: virtual_machine.go.
            Added: virtual_machine_delete_cloudinit_test.go,
            migration/v0.8.2.md.

2026-09-19  fix(client): every non-2xx response now returns the new
            exported type *StatusError. Before, 404, 409, 502, 503, 504
            and 595-599 were decoded as success. StatusError.Is maps
            404 to ErrNotFound and 401/403 to ErrNotAuthorized. The
            Error() text of the 400, 500 and 501 errors is unchanged.

            A non-2xx whose body cannot be read is a *StatusError
            too.

            Changed: proxmox.go, proxmox_test.go (a synthetic
            StatusCode 0 fixture set to 200), migration/v0.8.2.md,
            virtual_machine_delete_cloudinit_test.go.
            Added: status_error_test.go.

2026-09-19  fix(client): 500 and 501 errors now carry the response body
            in StatusError.Body. Their Error() text is unchanged.

            Changed: proxmox.go, status_error_test.go,
            migration/v0.8.2.md.

            These three changes are kept as separate commits on this
            fork's fixes branch, which carries no fork-specific content,
            so that each can be offered upstream as its own pull request.
